  "description_html": "Skeletal diagram of <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platytholus\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Platytholus\">Platytholus clemensi</a></i> showing known fossil material of the holotype specimen (<b>MOR 2915</b>). Scale bar=50 cm.\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Key\">Key</h3></div>\n<p><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#FFFFFF\" title=\"#FFFFFF\"> </b>=Holotype <small style=\"font-size:85%;\">(MOR 2915)</small><br>\n<b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#8C8C8C\" title=\"#8C8C8C\"> </b>=Unknown\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References\">References</h3></div>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080%2F02724634.2023.2190369\">\"A new pachycephalosaurid from the Hell Creek Formation, Garfield County, Montana, U.S.A.\"</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.palaeo.2017.11.029\">\"Morphology and histology of new cranial specimens of Pachycephalosauridae (Dinosauria: Ornithischia) from the Nemegt Formation, Mongolia\"</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.palaeontologia.pan.pl/Archive/1974_30_45-102_22-31.pdf\">\"Pachycephalosauria, a new suborder of ornithischian dinosaurs\"</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/getawaytrike/art/Stone-sand-ocean-707079640\"><i>Prenocephale</i> skeletal</a> by GetAwayTrike</li>\n<li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\" id=\"Reference-Paul-2016\">Paul, Gregory S. (2016)      <i> The Princeton Field Guide to Dinosaurs</i> (2nd ed.), Princeton, N.J.:  Princeton University Press  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"